  "notes": "The root of everything that stands on two legs and carries something in its hands. It is form, not finish: plain plates in neutral greys, named by what they are for (body, limb, dark, face, foot), so a child that gives nothing but five colours and a few extra ops is a different person. Shaped like a jointed print-in-place figurine: limbs two voxels across and held clear of the trunk, a dark joint between every pair of segments, a narrow waist and a box for a head, because a fighter is read at twenty metres by its gaps and a solid barrel of limbs reads as nothing. Eighteen bones, three to a limb, because this rig is driven by a player's movement rather than by an activity table and has to look right strafing, jumping, landing and dying as well as walking. Nothing lists it in a biome, so it only ever appears where code asks for it by name (the shooter's bots, the EDIT page).",
